  "question": "What did Rome trade with the Kingdom of Aksum?",
  "question_lang": null,
  "answer": "The sources retrieved do not answer this question. The sources do describe Roman trade with Aksum (the Kingdom of Zoskales): \"There are imported into these places, undressed cloth made in Egypt for the Berbers... wine of Laodicea and Italy, not much; olive oil, not much; for the king, gold and silver plate made after the fashion of the country\" [S1], and \"Φέρεται δὲ ἀπὸ τῶν τόπων ἐλέφας καὶ χελώνη καὶ ῥινόκερως\" [S4], but no English translation is available for the second passage, and the first passage does not specify what Aksum exported to Rome in return.",
